## DOT inspection services

We run the full federal DOT inspection, the one that keeps a fleet compliant and
roadworthy rather than a walk-around that produces a sticker. It covers:

- Comprehensive brake system inspections
- Tire condition and pressure checks
- Steering mechanism inspections
- Suspension system inspections
- Lights and reflectors inspections
- Windshield wiper checks

## Why the inspection matters

A DOT inspection is the annual proof that the parts a driver cannot see are
still within spec — brakes, tires, steering, lights. Finding a defect on the
rack is cheap. Finding it at a roadside stop costs the load, and finding it on
the road costs more than that. Regular inspections keep the fleet compliant and
keep the business out of the fines that follow a failed one.

{% callout tone="note" title="Book ahead of the expiry date" %}
An inspection booked the week it expires is an inspection with no room for a
repair. Bring the unit in early enough that anything we find can be fixed
before the certificate lapses.
{% /callout %}

